IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 65 to 69 -- ENDORSEMENT:
-- who is an appropriate person to endorse, when an endorsement is made, special and blank endorsements,
-- the effect of an unauthorized endorsement, and the warranties of a guarantor of a signature or of an
-- endorsement. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs. Across
-- modules a plain input stands in for the other rule's result, and the comment names the rule that works it
-- out: the rules for s 65 take about a dozen facts about one endorser, and the questions in ss 51, 76 and 77
-- do not otherwise ask them.

§ `s 65 Endorsement`

§§ `s 65(1) Definition of appropriate person`

-- Paragraphs (a) to (f) describe a person by their own facts. Paragraph (g) describes the authorized agent
-- or mandatary of a person described in (a) to (f), which is another person's facts: the caller works
-- those out with the rule below and passes the result as `the principal is a person described in
-- paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)`.
-- src:934 | 65 (1) In this section, appropriate person means
-- src:935 | (a) the person specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security;
-- src:936 | (b) if a person described in paragraph (a) is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity, either that person or the person’s successor;
-- src:937 | (c) if the security or endorsement mentioned in paragraph (a) specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity, the remaining fiduciary or fiduciaries, whether or not a successor has been appointed or qualified;
-- src:938 | (d) if a person described in paragraph (a) is an individual and is without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability, the person’s fiduciary;
-- src:939 | (e) if the security or endorsement mentioned in paragraph (a) specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign, the survivor or survivors;
-- src:940 | (f) a person having power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney; or
@ref CBCA s 65(1)(a)-(f) (src:934-940)
GIVEN `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the successor of that fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the fiduciary of that individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)` MEANS
        `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security`
    OR  (    `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity`
         AND (   `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving`
              OR `the person is the successor of that fiduciary`))
    OR  (    `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity`
         AND `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries`)
    OR  (    `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability`
         AND `the person is the fiduciary of that individual`)
    OR  (    `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign`
         AND `the person is a survivor`)
    OR  `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney`

-- src:934 | 65 (1) In this section, appropriate person means
-- src:935 | (a) the person specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security;
-- src:936 | (b) if a person described in paragraph (a) is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity, either that person or the person’s successor;
-- src:937 | (c) if the security or endorsement mentioned in paragraph (a) specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity, the remaining fiduciary or fiduciaries, whether or not a successor has been appointed or qualified;
-- src:938 | (d) if a person described in paragraph (a) is an individual and is without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability, the person’s fiduciary;
-- src:939 | (e) if the security or endorsement mentioned in paragraph (a) specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign, the survivor or survivors;
-- src:940 | (f) a person having power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney; or
-- src:941 | (g) to the extent that a person described in paragraphs (a) to (f) may act through an agent or mandatary, the authorized agent or mandatary.
@ref CBCA s 65(1) (src:934-941)
GIVEN `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the successor of that fiduciary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the fiduciary of that individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal is a person described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal may act through an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the authorized agent or mandatary of the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an appropriate person within s 65(1)` MEANS
        `the person is described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f) within s 65(1)`
            `the person is specified by the security or by special endorsement to be entitled to the security`
            `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is described as a fiduciary but is no longer serving in the described capacity`
            `the person is that fiduciary who is no longer serving`
            `the person is the successor of that fiduciary`
            `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person as fiduciaries and one or more are no longer serving in the described capacity`
            `the person is one of the remaining fiduciaries`
            `a person specified by the security or by special endorsement is an individual without capacity to act by reason of death, minority or incapability`
            `the person is the fiduciary of that individual`
            `the security or endorsement specifies more than one person with right of survivorship and by reason of death all cannot sign`
            `the person is a survivor`
            `the person has power to sign under applicable law or a power of attorney`
    OR  (    `the principal is a person described in paragraphs 65(1)(a) to (f)`
         AND `the principal may act through an agent or mandatary`
         AND `the person is the authorized agent or mandatary of the principal`)

§§ `s 65(2) Determining appropriate person`

-- The test is made as of the time of signing, and a later change of circumstances does not make the
-- endorsement unauthorized: so the only fact asked is whether the person was an appropriate person then.
-- src:943 | (2) Whether the person signing is an appropriate person is determined as of the time of signing and an endorsement by such a person does not become unauthorized for the purposes of this Part by reason of any subsequent change of circumstances.
@ref CBCA s 65(2) (src:943)
GIVEN `the person signing was an appropriate person at the time of signing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endorsement is authorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(2)` MEANS
    `the person signing was an appropriate person at the time of signing`

§§ `s 65(3) Endorsement`

-- src:945 | (3) An endorsement of a security in registered form is made when an appropriate person signs, either on the security or on a separate document, an assignment or transfer of the security or a power to assign or transfer it, or when the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security.
@ref CBCA s 65(3) (src:945)
GIVEN `the security is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appropriate person signs an assignment or transfer of the security, or a power to assign or transfer it, on the security or on a separate document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an endorsement of a security in registered form is made within s 65(3)` MEANS
        `the security is in registered form`
    AND (   `an appropriate person signs an assignment or transfer of the security, or a power to assign or transfer it, on the security or on a separate document`
         OR `the signature of an appropriate person is written without more on the back of the security`)

§§ `s 65(4) to (6) Special or blank`

-- A special endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to
-- transfer it (s 65(6)). An endorsement in blank includes an endorsement to bearer (s 65(5)). The text does
-- not say what else is "in blank", so an endorsement that is neither is not classified (fork F-P7-8).
-- src:947 | (4) An endorsement may be special or in blank.
-- src:948 | Blank endorsement
-- src:949 | (5) An endorsement in blank includes an endorsement to bearer.
-- src:950 | Special endorsement
-- src:951 | (6) A special endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it.
@ref CBCA s 65(4) (src:947-951)
GIVEN `the endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the endorsement is to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of endorsement`
`the kind of an endorsement within s 65(4)` MEANS
    IF `the endorsement specifies the person to whom the security is to be transferred, or who has power to transfer it`
    THEN JUST `a special endorsement`
    ELSE IF `the endorsement is to bearer`
         THEN JUST `an endorsement in blank`
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 65(7) Right of holder`

-- src:953 | (7) A holder may convert an endorsement in blank into a special endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 65(7) (src:953)
GIVEN `the person is a holder of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of the endorsement` IS A `Kind of endorsement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holder may convert the endorsement into a special endorsement within s 65(7)` MEANS
        `the person is a holder of the security`
    AND `the kind of the endorsement` EQUALS `an endorsement in blank`

§§ `s 65(8) Immunity of endorser`

-- src:955 | (8) Unless otherwise agreed, the endorser assumes no obligation that the security will be honoured by the issuer.
@ref CBCA s 65(8) (src:955)
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endorser assumes no obligation that the security will be honoured by the issuer within s 65(8)` MEANS
    NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`

§§ `s 65(9) Partial endorsement`

-- Effective "to the extent of the endorsement": the answer is the number of units for which it is effective.
-- NOTHING: the endorsement is not of part of a security of separately transferable units, so s 65(9)
-- says nothing about it.
-- src:957 | (9) An endorsement purporting to be only of part of a security representing units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable is effective to the extent of the endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 65(9) (src:957)
GIVEN `the endorsement purports to be only of part of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security represents units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of units the endorsement covers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of units for which the endorsement is effective within s 65(9)` MEANS
    IF     `the endorsement purports to be only of part of a security`
       AND `the security represents units intended by the issuer to be separately transferable`
    THEN JUST `the number of units the endorsement covers`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 65(10) Failure of fiduciary to comply`

-- NOTHING: the fiduciary did not fail to comply with a controlling instrument or law, so s 65(10) says nothing.
-- src:959 | (10) Failure of a fiduciary to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law of the jurisdiction governing the fiduciary relationship, including any law requiring the fiduciary to obtain court approval of a transfer, does not render the fiduciary’s endorsement unauthorized for the purposes of this Part.
@ref CBCA s 65(10) (src:959)
GIVEN `the fiduciary failed to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law governing the fiduciary relationship, including a law requiring court approval of a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the failure makes the fiduciary's endorsement unauthorized for the purposes of this Part within s 65(10)` MEANS
    IF `the fiduciary failed to comply with a controlling instrument or act or with the law governing the fiduciary relationship, including a law requiring court approval of a transfer`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 66 Effect of endorsement without delivery`

-- An endorsement does not constitute a transfer until delivery of the security on which it appears or, if the
-- endorsement is on a separate document, until delivery of both the security and that document.
-- src:961 | 66 An endorsement of a security whether special or in blank does not constitute a transfer until delivery of the security on which it appears or, if the endorsement is on a separate document, until delivery of both the security and that document.
@ref CBCA s 66 (src:961)
GIVEN `the security on which the endorsement appears has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the endorsement is on a separate document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the separate document has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endorsement constitutes a transfer within s 66` MEANS
        `the security on which the endorsement appears has been delivered`
    AND (   (NOT `the endorsement is on a separate document`)
         OR `the separate document has been delivered`)

§ `s 67 Endorsement in bearer form`

-- src:963 | 67 An endorsement of a security in bearer form may give notice of an adverse claim under section 61 but does not otherwise affect any right to registration that the holder has.
@ref CBCA s 67 (src:963)
GIVEN `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an endorsement of the security may give notice of an adverse claim under section 61 within s 67` MEANS
    `the security is in bearer form`

-- NOTHING: the security is not in bearer form, so s 67 says nothing about the holder's right to registration.
-- src:963 | 67 An endorsement of a security in bearer form may give notice of an adverse claim under section 61 but does not otherwise affect any right to registration that the holder has.
@ref CBCA s 67 (src:963)
GIVEN `the security is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an endorsement otherwise affects the holder's right to registration within s 67` MEANS
    IF `the security is in bearer form`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 68 Effect of unauthorized endorsement`

§§ `s 68(1) Effect of unauthorized endorsement`

-- src:965 | 68 (1) The owner of a security may assert the ineffectiveness of an endorsement against the issuer or any purchaser, other than a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer, unless the owner
-- src:966 | (a) has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security; or
-- src:967 | (b) is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 68(1) (src:965-967)
GIVEN `the endorsement is unauthorized or otherwise ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is the issuer or a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the endorsement against the other party within s 68(1)` MEANS
        `the endorsement is unauthorized or otherwise ineffective`
    AND `the other party is the issuer or a purchaser`
    AND (NOT `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice of an adverse claim who has in good faith received a new, reissued or re-registered security on registration of transfer`)
    AND (NOT `the owner has ratified an unauthorized endorsement of the security`)
    AND (NOT `the owner is otherwise precluded from impugning the effectiveness of an unauthorized endorsement`)

§§ `s 68(2) Liability of issuer`

-- src:968 | Liability of issuer
-- src:969 | (2) An issuer who registers the transfer of a security on an unauthorized endorsement is liable for improper registration.
@ref CBCA s 68(2) (src:968-969)
GIVEN `the issuer registered the transfer of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration was made on an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer is liable for improper registration within s 68(2)` MEANS
        `the issuer registered the transfer of the security`
    AND `the registration was made on an unauthorized endorsement`

§ `s 69 Warranties of guarantor`

§§ `s 69(1) Warranties of guarantor of signature`

-- src:971 | 69 (1) A person who guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security warrants that at the time of signing
-- src:972 | (a) the signature was genuine;
-- src:973 | (b) the signer was an appropriate person as defined in section 65 to endorse; and
-- src:974 | (c) the signer had legal capacity to sign.
@ref CBCA s 69(1) (src:971-974)
DECLARE `Warranty of a guarantor under s 69` IS ONE OF
    `a warranty that the signature was genuine at the time of signing`
    `a warranty that the signer was an appropriate person as defined in section 65 to endorse at the time of signing`
    `a warranty that the signer had legal capacity to sign at the time of signing`
    `a warranty of the rightfulness of the transfer in all respects`

-- NOTHING: the person does not guarantee a signature of an endorser.
-- src:971 | 69 (1) A person who guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security warrants that at the time of signing
-- src:972 | (a) the signature was genuine;
-- src:973 | (b) the signer was an appropriate person as defined in section 65 to endorse; and
-- src:974 | (c) the signer had legal capacity to sign.
@ref CBCA s 69(1) (src:971-974)
GIVEN `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty of a guarantor under s 69`)
`the warranties a guarantor of a signature gives within s 69(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty that the signature was genuine at the time of signing`,
                    `a warranty that the signer was an appropriate person as defined in section 65 to endorse at the time of signing`,
                    `a warranty that the signer had legal capacity to sign at the time of signing`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 69(2) Limitation of liability`

-- NOTHING: the person does not guarantee a signature of an endorser.
-- src:975 | Limitation of liability
-- src:976 | (2) A person who guarantees a signature of an endorser does not otherwise warrant the rightfulness of the particular transfer.
@ref CBCA s 69(2) (src:975-976)
GIVEN `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a guarantor of a signature warrants the rightfulness of the particular transfer within s 69(2)` MEANS
    IF `the person guarantees a signature of an endorser of a security`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 69(3) Warranties of guarantor of endorsement`

-- NOTHING: the person does not guarantee an endorsement of a security.
-- src:977 | Warranties of guarantor of endorsement
-- src:978 | (3) A person who guarantees an endorsement of a security warrants both the signature and the rightfulness of the transfer in all respects, but an issuer may not require a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer.
@ref CBCA s 69(3) (src:977-978)
GIVEN `the person guarantees an endorsement of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty of a guarantor under s 69`)
`the warranties a guarantor of an endorsement gives within s 69(3)` MEANS
    IF `the person guarantees an endorsement of a security`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty that the signature was genuine at the time of signing`,
                    `a warranty that the signer was an appropriate person as defined in section 65 to endorse at the time of signing`,
                    `a warranty that the signer had legal capacity to sign at the time of signing`,
                    `a warranty of the rightfulness of the transfer in all respects`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- An issuer may not require a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer.
-- NOTHING: the issuer requires no guarantee of endorsement, so s 69(3) says nothing.
-- src:977 | Warranties of guarantor of endorsement
-- src:978 | (3) A person who guarantees an endorsement of a security warrants both the signature and the rightfulness of the transfer in all respects, but an issuer may not require a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer.
@ref CBCA s 69(3) (src:977-978)
GIVEN `the issuer requires a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the issuer's requirement of a guarantee of endorsement is permitted within s 69(3)` MEANS
    IF `the issuer requires a guarantee of endorsement as a condition to registration of transfer`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 69(4) Extent of liability`

-- src:979 | Extent of liability
-- src:980 | (4) The warranties referred to in this section are made to any person taking or dealing with the security relying on the guarantee and the guarantor is liable to such person for any loss resulting from breach of warranty.
@ref CBCA s 69(4) (src:979-980)
GIVEN `the person takes or deals with the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person relies on the guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the warranties are made to the person within s 69(4)` MEANS
        `the person takes or deals with the security`
    AND `the person relies on the guarantee`

-- The guarantor is liable for "any loss resulting from breach of warranty". The answer is the amount of
-- that loss. NOTHING: the warranties are not made to the person, or no warranty was breached.
-- src:979 | Extent of liability
-- src:980 | (4) The warranties referred to in this section are made to any person taking or dealing with the security relying on the guarantee and the guarantor is liable to such person for any loss resulting from breach of warranty.
@ref CBCA s 69(4) (src:979-980)
GIVEN `the person takes or deals with the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person relies on the guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warranty referred to in section 69 was breached` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss resulting from the breach in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the guarantor's liability to the person in dollars within s 69(4)` MEANS
    IF     `the warranties are made to the person within s 69(4)`
               `the person takes or deals with the security`
               `the person relies on the guarantee`
       AND `a warranty referred to in section 69 was breached`
    THEN JUST `the loss resulting from the breach in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING
